# ── Libris — TiDB connection configuration ─────────────────────────────
#
# The app talks to TWO SEPARATE TiDB deployments:
#   • BOOKS_DATABASE_URL → books + pages (cluster A)
#   • NOTES_DATABASE_URL → margin notes + board notes (cluster B)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own clusters.
# Prisma is used with the MySQL connector (TiDB is MySQL-compatible).
#
# ── Option 1 · TiDB Cloud (recommended for production) ──────────────────────
# Create TWO clusters (or one cluster + two databases on different tiers is
# NOT recommended — the point is independence). Get the connection string
# from each cluster's "Connect" panel and append sslaccept=strict for TLS:
#
# BOOKS_DATABASE_URL="mysql://<user>:<password>@<host-a>:4000/books_db?sslaccept=strict"
# NOTES_DATABASE_URL="mysql://<user>:<password>@<host-b>:4000/notes_db?sslaccept=strict"
#
# ── Option 2 · Self-hosted TiDB (two tiup playground clusters) ──────────────
# Start two local clusters, then create the databases (see README.md):
#
BOOKS_DATABASE_URL="mysql://root@127.0.0.1:4000/books_db"
NOTES_DATABASE_URL="mysql://root@127.0.0.1:4001/notes_db"
#
# (Optional) Legacy single default — points at the books cluster.
DATABASE_URL="mysql://root@127.0.0.1:4000/books_db"

# ── CockroachDB backup engine (snapshots, overflow, activity logs) ────────
# When TiDB storage is under 10MB remaining, newly written notes & books
# directly shift to the CockroachDB backup engine without downtime.
# (The old Turso backup DB is decommissioned — these vars are dead.)
# BACKUP_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=verify-full"

# ── API auth gate (C-1/H-2/H-3 fix) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Empty = PUBLIC OPEN MODE (this app is intentionally public: anyone can
# read/write/delete). Set ONLY to lock down a private deployment — then every
# /api route requires `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32  (min 16 chars enforced)
# ADMIN_TOKEN="<64-hex-chars>"
# Client retries can send idempotency keys: header `x-idempotency-key: <uuid>`
# Destructive restore additionally requires body {"confirm":"RESTORE"}.
# Drift repair: POST /api/storage {"action":"repair"}.

# ── Live quota probe (shift engine) ──────────────────────────────────────
# By default remaining TiDB space is probed live via information_schema
# (60s cache). Overrides for testing / manual control:
# TIDB_QUOTA_BYTES=5368709120
# TIDB_BOOKS_REMAINING_BYTES=5368672212
# TIDB_NOTES_REMAINING_BYTES=5368672503

# ── Users store — third TiDB cluster (display names, PINs, presence, leases)
# USERS_DATABASE_URL="mysql://<user>:<password>@<host-c>:4000/users_db?sslaccept=strict"
# Dashboard ceiling defaults to the TiDB Starter allowance (5 GiB row storage)
# — override if the cluster is on a paid plan:
# USERS_QUOTA_BYTES=5368709120

# ── CockroachDB backup engine ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Snapshots, restore source, shift overflow, replication mirror, activity logs.
# BACKUP_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://<user>:<password>@<host>:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=verify-full"
# Quota honesty: the dashboard byte counts are MEASURED content bytes
# (octet_length sums in SQL). The ceiling defaults to the CockroachDB Cloud
# Basic free allowance (10 GiB/month, cockroachlabs.com/pricing) — override
# it if your cluster is on a paid plan:
# BACKUP_QUOTA_BYTES=10737418240

# ── Distributed rate limiting (optional) ─────────────────────────────────
# Without these, limits are per-process memory (fine for single instance).
# Set both to share counters across Vercel/serverless instances:
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL="https://<your-db>.upstash.io"
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN="<your-token>"

# ── Prisma pool (optional, Wave E) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults are adequate at this scale. If TiDB reports connection pressure,
# append ?connection_limit=5 to the DATABASE_URLs (applies per client).
# Prisma clients + the UsrInfo libsql client are cached on globalThis in all envs.

# ── Destructive scripts (Wave A) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# seed / clear-notes / restore-demo refuse to run unless explicitly armed:
# ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_SCRIPT=1 npm run seed
